#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
somna: nightly memory curation for Claude Code, on your Mac.

Each night Somna reads your recent Claude Code sessions and proposes an updated,
curated memory. You review the change, then adopt or discard it.

How a cycle works:
  Somna reads your current memory and your recent sessions, and proposes an updated
  copy on a git branch. Your current memory is not touched until you adopt the copy.

Context per repo and client:
  - repos are discovered from sessions and mapped to clients (engine/repos.json)
  - every repo gets a context file under memory/clients/<client>/repos/<repo>.md
  - a SessionStart hook injects that context into Claude Code sessions in the repo
  - agents append updates to memory/inbox/<client>/<repo>.md, the cycle curates them
  - one scoped engine run per client, so client knowledge never crosses clients
  - structured logs for every decision (logs/somna.jsonl, logs/somna.log)

It also offers:
  - per-cycle instructions, model and explicit session ids, cancel, typed errors
  - live event stream and token usage while a cycle runs, memory reads/writes visible
  - version list and redact for memory files, read-only memory for agents,
    instructions per attached context, and trying a proposal before adopting it

Needs only the Python standard library (3.9+), git, and the Claude Code CLI.
"""
